                <pb facs="0463" n="453" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg453"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">390.1115A/633: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul at Foochow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Rice</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-12-30T23:00:00-05:00">December 30,
                            1941—11 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>17. Your December 27, 6 p.m. Department approves the action you contemplate in
                    informing American citizens residing in your district of the potential danger of
                    continued residence therein. If in your considered opinion the danger of
                    continued residence at Foochow and certain coastal sections of your district is
                    greater than the present risks of travel to places of greater safety elsewhere,
                    you should not hesitate to advise American citizens to avail themselves of the
                    present opportunities to withdraw from potential danger zones.</p>
                <p>Department has communicated the sense of your telegram under reference to the
                    mission boards mentioned therein and is now awaiting their decision respecting
                    the instructions to be given to their missionaries in the Foochow district.
                    These instructions will be communicated to you as soon as they are received.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
